# MedSync Health, Inc.
## Performance Review Policy
**Document ID**: HR-006
**Classification**: Internal
**Effective Date**: January 1, 2025

---

## Overview

MedSync Health's performance management system is designed to support employee growth, recognize contributions, and align individual performance with company objectives. This document outlines the processes and expectations for performance reviews.

---

## Performance Review Cycle

### Annual Review Timeline

| Phase | Timing | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| Goal Setting | January | Set annual OKRs aligned to company goals |
| Q1 Check-in | April | Progress review, feedback exchange |
| Mid-Year Review | July | Formal checkpoint, goal adjustment |
| Q3 Check-in | October | Progress review, development focus |
| Annual Review | February | Comprehensive evaluation, compensation decisions |

### New Hire Reviews
- 30-day check-in: Manager informal feedback
- 60-day check-in: Performance tracking
- 90-day review: Formal evaluation (pass/fail for probation)

---

## Performance Ratings

### Rating Scale

| Rating | Definition | % of Employees |
|--------|------------|----------------|
| **Exceptional** | Consistently exceeds all expectations; role model | ~5% |
| **Exceeds** | Exceeds expectations in most areas | ~20% |
| **Meets** | Fully meets expectations; solid performer | ~55% |
| **Developing** | Partially meets expectations; improvement needed | ~15% |
| **Below** | Does not meet expectations; requires action plan | ~5% |

### Calibration Process
1. Manager submits initial ratings
2. Department calibration sessions
3. Cross-functional leadership calibration
4. Executive review of top/bottom ratings
5. Final ratings approved by HR

---

## Review Components

### Self-Assessment
All employees complete self-assessment covering:
- Key accomplishments vs. goals
- Challenges and learnings
- Collaboration and values demonstration
- Development needs

### Manager Assessment

| Category | Weight |
|----------|--------|
| Results/OKR Achievement | 40% |
| Skills & Competencies | 25% |
| Values Demonstration | 20% |
| Growth & Development | 15% |

### 360-Degree Feedback
- Required for M1+ levels
- Optional for IC3+ levels
- Minimum 3 peer reviewers
- Direct report feedback for managers

---

## Goals and OKRs

### Goal-Setting Guidelines
- 3-5 objectives per quarter
- At least one stretch goal
- Aligned to department and company OKRs
- Specific, measurable outcomes

### Sample OKR Format

**Objective**: Improve customer onboarding experience

| Key Result | Target | Weight |
|------------|--------|--------|
| Reduce time-to-value from 45 to 30 days | 30 days | 40% |
| Increase implementation NPS from 42 to 55 | 55 NPS | 35% |
| Achieve 95% on-time go-live rate | 95% | 25% |

