## Compensation Decisions

### Merit Increase Guidelines

| Rating | Typical Increase | Exceptional Cases |
|--------|-----------------|-------------------|
| Exceptional | 8-12% | Up to 15% |
| Exceeds | 5-8% | Up to 10% |
| Meets | 3-5% | Up to 6% |
| Developing | 0-2% | — |
| Below | 0% | — |

### Equity Refresh

| Rating | Refresh (% of Initial Grant) |
|--------|------------------------------|
| Exceptional | 40-50% |
| Exceeds | 25-35% |
| Meets | 15-25% |
| Developing | 0-10% |
| Below | 0% |

### Promotion Criteria
- Minimum 12 months in current role
- Consistently performing at next level
- Rating of "Meets" or above for 2 consecutive cycles
- Manager recommendation with VP approval

---

## Performance Improvement

### Performance Improvement Plan (PIP)

For employees rated "Below Expectations":

| Phase | Duration | Actions |
|-------|----------|---------|
| Verbal Warning | 2 weeks | Documented conversation, expectations reset |
| Written Warning | 4 weeks | Formal PIP document, weekly check-ins |
| Final Review | 4 weeks | Demonstrate improvement or separation |

### PIP Requirements
- Specific, measurable improvement goals
- Weekly manager check-ins
- HR oversight
- Documentation of all interactions
- Clear consequences for non-improvement

---

## Manager Responsibilities

### Ongoing Duties
- Weekly 1:1s with direct reports
- Quarterly goal check-ins
- Real-time feedback (positive and constructive)
- Document performance throughout the year

### Review Period Duties
- Complete assessments on time
- Participate in calibration sessions
- Deliver feedback in person
- Submit compensation recommendations

### Manager Rating Consideration
Managers are evaluated on:
- Team performance outcomes
- Employee engagement scores
- Retention of high performers
- Development of direct reports

---

## Employee Rights

### Feedback and Appeals
- Employees may respond in writing to reviews
- Disagreements escalated to HR Business Partner
- Appeal process for disputed ratings
- No retaliation for good-faith concerns

### Confidentiality
- Reviews are confidential personnel records
- Access limited to HR, manager, and skip-level
- Employees receive copy of their review

